    <briefdescription>
<para>30/360 day count convention </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The 30/360 day count can be calculated according to US, European, or Italian conventions.</para><para>US (NASD) convention: if the starting date is the 31st of a month, it becomes equal to the 30th of the same month. If the ending date is the 31st of a month and the starting date is earlier than the 30th of a month, the ending date becomes equal to the 1st of the next month, otherwise the ending date becomes equal to the 30th of the same month. Also known as &quot;30/360&quot;, &quot;360/360&quot;, or &quot;Bond Basis&quot;</para><para>European convention: starting dates or ending dates that occur on the 31st of a month become equal to the 30th of the same month. Also known as &quot;30E/360&quot;, or &quot;Eurobond Basis&quot;</para><para>Italian convention: starting dates or ending dates that occur on February and are grater than 27 become equal to 30 for computational sake. </para>    </detaileddescription>
